infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title ESM-only vs dual-publish (ESM + CJS)
  desc One module instance, or the dual-package hazard
  compares
    - label ESM-only
      children
        - label One module instance
          desc Single copy loaded; the hazard cannot arise
        - label instanceof works
          desc One class identity across the boundary
        - label Singletons stay single
          desc Module-level cache/registry not duplicated
        - label Strongest tree-shaking
          desc Static imports let bundlers drop dead code
        - label Cost: drops pure-CJS
          desc They cannot require() without await import()
    - label Dual-publish (ESM + CJS)
      children
        - label Two module instances
          desc A graph can load both copies at once
        - label instanceof breaks
          desc Two class identities across the boundary
        - label State silently duplicated
          desc Caches, registries, singletons split in two
        - label Maximum reach
          desc Serves old CJS and modern ESM consumers
        - label Needs one internal core
          desc Both wrappers must re-export shared state
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
